Package: ${PACKAGE_NAME}
Version: $VERSION
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: $INSTALLED_SIZE
Depends: bash (>= 5), parted, e2fsprogs, rsync, whiptail, dosfstools, fdisk, curl
Recommends: bash-completion
Suggests: pv, jq, lsof, btrfs-progs, f2fs-tools, mailutils, default-mta | msmtp-mta | mail-transport-agent
Maintainer: framp <framp@linux-tips-and-tricks.de>
Homepage: https://raspibackup.linux-tips-and-tricks.de
Description: Backup your Raspberry Pi systems
 Create and keep multiple backup versions of your running Raspberries
 with dd, tar or rsync. Backups are restored to a new SD card, USB disk
 or SSD with raspiBackup itself.
 .
 raspiBackupConfig configures the backup, its schedule with a systemd
 timer, the number of backup versions to keep and email notifications.
 Extensions run your own code before and after a backup.
